    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McGuirk Beggan Property are delighted to present this charming 1940s red brick home to the market, a beautifully maintained property that combines the character and proportions of its era with stylish modern interiors and exciting potential for further development.\n\nFrom the moment you step inside, it is clear that this is a home that has been cared for and decorated with great flair. Presented in excellent decorative condition throughout, the property offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation together with the rare advantage of a large side garden/space providing superb potential to extend. The current owners have already commissioned some fabulous architectural designs, giving prospective purchasers a wonderful opportunity to see just how much more could be achieved with this impressive property.\n\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully laid out and has been extended to the rear, creating generous living space for modern family life. The welcoming living room features a beautiful bay window & timber floors, while the kitchen/dining area is bright, stylish and well equipped, with ample room for family dining and entertaining. French doors open out to the sunny rear garden.\n\nUpstairs there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, together with a fully tiled family bathroom featuring an electric shower.\n\nOutside, the property enjoys a sunny south-east facing rear garden, designed for ease of maintenance and providing an excellent private outdoor space. A large shed offers excellent additional storage, while the generous space to the side presents a real opportunity to create something truly special, subject of course to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nPerfectly positioned just off the Crumlin Road, the property is within easy reach of a host of local shops, schools, bus routes and an abundance of amenities. Crumlin, Kimmage, Walkinstown and the surrounding areas offer an excellent choice of cafés, restaurants, shopping facilities, sporting clubs and recreational amenities, while the city centre is readily accessible by a number of bus routes.\n\nThis is a wonderful opportunity to acquire a characterful red-brick home in excellent condition, with stylish interiors, generous accommodation and outstanding potential to extend further. The combination of its superb location, south-east facing garden, off-street parking and exciting architectural possibilities makes this a home that is sure to appeal to a wide range of buyers.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate what this impressive home has to offer.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
